    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a potent offensive core led by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, who anchors our projections with a 64.35 efficiency score against the right-handed delivery of Elder. While his raw base is strong, his matchup benefits from a favorable xERA of 4.12, providing a high ceiling for run production. Our most efficient start is **Jackson Merrill** (62.07), who finds himself in a prime spot against Nola. Despite Nola\u2019s tendency to hold runners, **Jackson Merrill**\u2019s ability to leverage a dynamic platoon advantage (+13%) makes him a must-start, paired alongside **Kyle Tucker** (61.08) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (61.04). **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** specifically capitalizes on the favorable matchup against Bachar, where his platoon advantage provides the necessary boost to remain a core contributor.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Coby Mayo**, who landed just outside our starting nine with a 48.16 score. While **Coby Mayo** benefits from a strong park factor and a decent platoon outlook against Early, his efficiency is suppressed by the elite skill level of the opposing starter, and he ultimately lacks the projected volume of higher-scored options like **Josh Jung** (55.18). We are also navigating caution regarding **Gunnar Henderson** (50.92); despite his elite talent, his score is tempered by a significant 15% penalty due to the high skill level of Early, necessitating a conservative approach to preserve game caps. \n\nRisk management remains a priority given the volatility of our lower-tier starters. **Liam Hicks** (45.50) and **Dominic Smith** (45.39) occupy the bottom of our active lineup, serving as marginal plays that require careful monitoring. We continue to hold **Luis Robert Jr.** on the IL, and while players like **Brayan Rocchio** were considered, his sub-40 floor score cemented his place on the bench to protect our roster efficiency. As the lineup becomes official, we remain hyper-focused on maintaining our stolen base ceiling while avoiding unnecessary exposure to the league's elite arms.",
